# 🐧 11. Linux Mounting

## What is Mounting?

Mounting makes a filesystem available at a directory location within the Linux filesystem hierarchy.

Example:

```text
/dev/sdb1
   ↓
mount
   ↓
/mnt/data
```

Once mounted, users and applications can access the filesystem through the mount point.

### Useful commands

```bash
mount
```

Shows mounted filesystems.

```bash
findmnt
```

Shows mounted filesystems in a structured format.

```bash
lsblk
```

Displays block devices and their filesystem information.

### Interview Answer

> Mounting makes a filesystem accessible through a directory in the Linux filesystem hierarchy.

