# 13. Linux `sudoers`

The sudoers configuration determines which users and groups are permitted to use `sudo` and under what conditions.

Main file:

```text
/etc/sudoers
```

A safer editing method is:

```bash
sudo visudo
```

### Why this matters

It provides controlled privilege escalation.

### Example

```bash
sudo systemctl restart ssh
```

### Interview Answer

> The sudoers configuration defines which users or groups are authorized to use sudo and what commands they can execute with elevated privileges.

