# 17. Access Port vs Trunk Port

## Access Port

An access port typically carries traffic for one VLAN.

```text
PC
 ↓
Access Port
 ↓
VLAN 10
```

## Trunk Port

A trunk port can carry traffic for multiple VLANs between network devices.

```text
Switch A
   ⇅
 Trunk
   ⇅
Switch B
```

### Memory

```text
Access → One VLAN
Trunk  → Multiple VLANs
```

### Important

Do not confuse:

```text
VLAN
≠
VPN
```

